"cmake ..\n"
"make lidar_node\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:399
msgid "Run the node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:401
msgid "Run the node from terminal 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:403
msgid "./build/lidar_node\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:407
msgid "Run the world from terminal 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:409
msgid "gz sim sensor_tutorial.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:413
msgid ""
"Now you can see the robot move forward and as it approaches the wall it "
"starts to turn left until it's clear and moves forward again (be sure to "
"press the play button in the bottom-left corner to make the robot start "
"moving)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:415
msgid "Gazebo launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:417
msgid ""
"Instead of running two different tasks from two different terminals we can "
"make a launch file which will run the `sensor_world` and the `lidar_node` at "
"the same time. Open your text editor and add the following code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:419
msgid ""
"<?xml version='1.0'?>\n"
"<gz version='1.0'>\n"
"  <executable name='sensor-world'>\n"
"    <command>gz sim sensor_tutorial.sdf</command>\n"
"  </executable>\n"
"\n"
"  <executable name='lidar_node'>\n"
"    <command>./build/lidar_node</command>\n"
"  </executable>\n"
"\n"
"</gz>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:433
msgid ""
"The launch file is an XML file. We simply define what commands will run "
"under the `<executable>` tag. The first command is `gz sim sensor_tutorial."
"sdf` which launches the world. And the second command is `./build/"
"lidar_node` which runs the `lidar_node`. Save the file as `sensor_launch."
"gzlaunch`, and then run it using the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:438
msgid "gz launch sensor_launch.gzlaunch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sensors.md:442
msgid ""
"Press the play button to start the simulation. Hurray! Our robot is now "
"moving and avoiding the wall."
msgstr ""

